    "victims of") and agent nouns ending in -er/-or: strongly positive;
  * after degree, level, rank or extent nouns ("level of", "degree of", "center of",
    "front of", "lot of", "out of", "terms of", "species of"): strongly positive;
  * after plural nouns: mildly positive;
  * after quantity and partitive nouns ("number of", "part of", "one of", "some of",
    "instance of", "kind of", "amount of", "percent of"): about zero;
  * after mathematical, statistical or structural nouns and after "consist" / "think"
    ("array of", "grid of", "matrix of", "list of", "range of", "distribution of",
    "consists of", "think of"): strongly negative;
  * after a few quantifiers and abstract nouns ("all of", "each of", "end of", "time of",
    "variety of", "history of", "view of", "effect of"): mildly negative.
Every other token predicts 0. A word not listed in any group above gets about 0.15.
"""

