Recognize location-question and indefinite-location words across languages.
Chinese compounds weaken the response: locative uses retain more of it than
processing/handling uses. Numbers below are strengths estimated on training
text. This uses token spelling, not sentence meaning; byte-split characters
are recognized when completed. Other token-specific responses are omitted.
"""
